      "sc:author": "Fishka Bio",
      "sc:citation": {
        "@id": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21444547"
      },
      "sc:description": "Browser-based viewer for Sanger sequencing chromatograms in AB1/ABIF and SCF format. Opens .ab1/.abi/.fsa files, shows raw and analysed traces, basecalls, quality values and the ABIF directory, and puts two reads side by side for comparison. Aligns a read against a reference sequence to highlight mismatches. Drag on a trace to select a base range, then copy it as FASTA, zoom to it or export just that region. Exports the read as FASTA, FASTQ or ABIF and the chromatogram as a high-resolution image. Open files are kept as local sessions, so a closed tab can be picked up where it was left. Runs entirely in the browser — files are never uploaded.",
      "sc:featureList": [
        {
          "@id": "edam:operation_0491"
        },
        {
          "@id": "edam:operation_3203"
        }
      ],
